    },
    {
      "muscleGroup": "shoulders",
      "severity": "mild",
      "observation": "Shoulders were trained with just 2 sets at 5.2% of total volume, and the strength index has been flat at 101. Shoulder health is closely tied to back training movements, so keeping at least minimal direct shoulder work is worthwhile for joint integrity and balanced development."
    }
  ],
  "deloadRecommended": false,
  "deloadReason": null,
  "actionItems": [
    "Continue prioritizing back volume at or around 12 sets per period — this is clearly working, as the strength index rose 4 points this week. Stay the course on exercises that are driving that progress.",
    "Add 1 to 2 sets of direct shoulder work next period to support joint health and prevent the shoulder strength index from falling behind over time.",
    "Consider adding at least 1 additional chest set next period. Even a small maintenance stimulus will help prevent a growing imbalance as your back continues to develop.",
    "Monitor recovery closely as the last period's note flagged it. If performance on back exercises starts to feel flat or your quality of work drops, that is an early signal to consider a lighter recovery week."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "Back strength index rose strongly from 106 to 110 with 12 sets and dominant volume at 55.6%; all other groups were flat but stable, and mild imbalances in chest and shoulders should be watched going forward."
}
